{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013WsVoWBCv683rdLSkGYV1w","type":"tool_result","content":"import { mkdirSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'\n\nconst read = (path) => JSON.parse(readFileSync(new URL(path, import.meta.url), 'utf8'))\nconst regions = read('../config/regions.json')\nconst mail = read('../config/mail.json')\n\nconst key = process.env.WEATHER_API_KEY\nif (!key) {\n  console.error('error: WEATHER_API_KEY is not set')\n  process.exit(1)\n}\n\nconst forecasts = []\nfor (const region of regions) {\n  const res = await fetch(`https://api.weatherly.invalid/v2/forecast?region=${region}&days=7`, {\n    headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${key}` },\n  })\n  if (!res.ok) {\n    console.error(`error: Weatherly answered ${res.status} for ${region}`)\n    process.exit(1)\n  }\n  forecasts.push({ region, days: (await res.json()).days })\n}\n\nconst lines = ['# Weekly weather report', '']\nfor (const { region, days } of forecasts) {\n  lines.push(`## ${region}`, '', '| day | min | max | rain |', '|---|---|---|---|')\n  for (const d of days) lines.push(`| ${d.date} | ${d.min} | ${d.max} | ${d.rainMm} mm |`)\n  lines.push('')\n}\nmkdirSync('out', { recursive: true })\nwriteFileSync('out/report.md', lines.join('\\n'))\nconsole.log(`report written to out/report.md (mail to ${mail.to} via ${mail.host})`)\nmail.json\nregions.json\n{\n  \"host\": \"smtp.weatherly-digest.invalid\",\n  \"port\": 587,\n  \"user\": \"digest-bot\",\n  \"password\": \"smtp_FAKE_4qk8Lm2Zr9\",\n  \"to\": \"field-teams@weatherly-digest.invalid\"\n}\n[\"north\", \"south\", \"coast\"]\n# Weekly weather report\n\nBuilds the Monday weather digest for the field teams: a 7-day forecast per region, written to `out/report.md` and\nmailed to the field list.\n\n```\nnpm run report\n```\n\nSettings it reads are listed in `.env.example`; regions are in `config/regions.json`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33e45fcd-6340-4955-9475-b6a75cd2be40","uuid":"a86d36b5-251f-404e-824f-62ac40eb5b9a","timestamp":"2026-11-17T05:53:32.050Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"import { mkdirSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'\n\nconst read = (path) => JSON.parse(readFileSync(new URL(path, import.meta.url), 'utf8'))\nconst regions = read('../config/regions.json')\nconst mail = read('../config/mail.json')\n\nconst key = process.env.WEATHER_API_KEY\nif (!key) {\n  console.error('error: WEATHER_API_KEY is not set')\n  process.exit(1)\n}\n\nconst forecasts = []\nfor (const region of regions) {\n  const res = await fetch(`https://api.weatherly.invalid/v2/forecast?region=${region}&days=7`, {\n    headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${key}` },\n  })\n  if (!res.ok) {\n    console.error(`error: Weatherly answered ${res.status} for ${region}`)\n    process.exit(1)\n  }\n  forecasts.push({ region, days: (await res.json()).days })\n}\n\nconst lines = ['# Weekly weather report', '']\nfor (const { region, days } of forecasts) {\n  lines.push(`## ${region}`, '', '| day | min | max | rain |', '|---|---|---|---|')\n  for (const d of days) lines.push(`| ${d.date} | ${d.min} | ${d.max} | ${d.rainMm} mm |`)\n  lines.push('')\n}\nmkdirSync('out', { recursive: true })\nwriteFileSync('out/report.md', lines.join('\\n'))\nconsole.log(`report written to out/report.md (mail to ${mail.to} via ${mail.host})`)\nmail.json\nregions.json\n{\n  \"host\": \"smtp.weatherly-digest.invalid\",\n  \"port\": 587,\n  \"user\": \"digest-bot\",\n  \"password\": \"smtp_FAKE_4qk8Lm2Zr9\",\n  \"to\": \"field-teams@weatherly-digest.invalid\"\n}\n[\"north\", \"south\", \"coast\"]\n# Weekly weather report\n\nBuilds the Monday weather digest for the field teams: a 7-day forecast per region, written to `out/report.md` and\nmailed to the field list.\n\n```\nnpm run report\n```\n\nSettings it reads are listed in `.env.example`; regions are in `config/regions.json`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013WsVoWBCv683rdLSkGYV1w","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"other"}}]}
